<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Bansud issues $30 million note.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Bansud issues $30 million note.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine bank Bansud SA said Thursday it has sold $30 million in 180-day notes.</p>
<p>The notes, maturing on April 29, 1997, were sold at a price of 96.212. The issue was fully subscribed by Citibank International Plc, in its role as underwriter.</p>
<p>The notes were issued as part of Bansud's $400 million short-term negotiable bond program approved in August.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180668</p>
</text>
